Most breathing guides list techniques. Few tell you which one to use while you're actually wound up, or how strong the evidence is.

The short version: slow breathing at about 6 breaths a minute (try in for 4, out for 6) has the best support. The physiological sigh is the fastest reset. Box breathing and 4-7-8 are useful, but they have less direct research behind them. Most studies test 5 minutes, so one minute is a starting dose.

We wrote five 60-second scripts with exact counts, common mistakes and a real safety section. DeRot, our upcoming iOS app, builds this reset into the middle of the scroll. {url}
